WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
In 1930, Gandhi led the Salt March.

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:07.720
His weapon was truth-force,
with no violence at all.

3
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:13.050
In 1955, Martin Luther King helped
lead a bus boycott in Montgomery.

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.300
Yet critics ask: could non-violence
ever have stopped Hitler?

5
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.080
So is refusing to fight brave or naive?

6
00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:24.010
Why do some believers never use violence?

7
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.730
In this mission, you'll
place views on a scale,

8
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.860
from rejecting all violence to holy war.

9
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:34.990
Then you'll meet the Quakers, who
have refused outward wars since 1660.

10
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.240
Your mission: weigh up why some
believers will never use violence.
